<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 23 October, from 4004 BCE to 1983.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">4004 BCE <span class="tih-ago">6,029 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Archbishop Ussher's date for the Creation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In his chronology of 1650, Archbishop James Ussher calculated from biblical genealogies that the world was created on the evening before Sunday 23 October 4004 BCE. The date was printed in many English Bibles for two centuries.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-philippi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-philippi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/42-bce">42 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,067 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brutus takes his own life after defeat at Philippi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and Octavian in the second engagement at Philippi in Macedonia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-junius-brutus">Marcus Junius Brutus</a>, a leader of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s assassins, took his own life. The triumvirs' victory ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">the Liberators</a>' civil war and the republican cause.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-philippi">Battle of Philippi</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-junius-brutus">Marcus Junius Brutus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberators-civil-war">Liberators' civil war</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">502 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,524 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A synod at Palma refuses to judge Pope Symmachus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Urged by the Ostrogothic king Theodoric to settle the matter, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> met at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palma">Palma</a> and declared they could not judge Pope Symmachus, successor of Peter the Apostle, leaving it to God. The resolutions were signed by 76 bishops.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric the Great</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1086">1086 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">940 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Yusuf ibn Tashfin's Almoravids defeat Alfonso VI at Sagrajas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a>, the Almoravid army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a>, called in by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, shattered the forces of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI of Castile</a>. The victory preserved Muslim control of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> under Almoravid influence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sagrajas">Battle of Sagrajas</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1157">1157 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">869 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Valdemar I defeats Sweyn III at Grathe Heath</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vyborg">Viborg</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jutland">Jutland</a>, Valdemar I defeated his rival for the Danish throne, Sweyn III, who was killed while fleeing. The battle ended the Danish civil wars, and Valdemar became sole king.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-grathe-heath">Battle of Grathe Heath</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1295">1295 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">731 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Scotland and France seal the first treaty of the Auld Alliance</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A treaty between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-balliol">John Balliol</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-france">Philip IV of France</a>, signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auld-alliance">Auld Alliance</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. Renewed by most later Scottish kings, it drew Scotland into repeated wars with England and effectively ended in 1560.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auld-alliance">Auld Alliance</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1642">1642 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">384 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Royalists and Parliamentarians clash at Edgehill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles I's army fought Parliament's forces under the Earl of Essex at Edgehill in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warwickshire">Warwickshire</a>, the first pitched battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-civil-war">English Civil War</a>. The indecisive result made clear the war would be long.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1956">1956 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">70 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Hungarian Revolution begins in Budapest</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A student demonstration in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a> grew into a national uprising against the communist government and Soviet control. Soviet forces crushed it in November, leaving some 2,500 Hungarians dead and 200,000 in exile.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1983">1983 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">43 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Truck bombs kill 241 US and 58 French troops in Beirut</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Suicide bombers drove explosive-laden trucks into the US Marine barracks and a French paratroop building in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beirut">Beirut</a>. The attacks led to the withdrawal of the multinational peacekeeping force from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beirut">Beirut</a></div></div></li></ol>
